WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:02.230
- I think we have to give up on

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:03.230
person number three.

00:00:05.502 --> 00:00:08.085
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:10.910
Hi, I'm Inga.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.510
I really like bento boxes.

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:15.660
Recently, I found some
super, super, super cute ones

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.430
on the internet, so I
decided to challenge myself

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:21.110
to see if I can make a
super cute bento box.

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:22.830
I've never made bento boxes before.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.910
I definitely don't think
it's going to be easy.

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:28.360
I'm hoping that my bento box looks

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:29.780
at least a little bit presentable.

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:32.560
A bento box that hopefully
people will think

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:33.750
is too cute to eat.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:34.910
Alright, so let's go!

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:37.330
So the first step before
I did anything else

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:38.910
was to buy a bento box.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:40.450
Ta-da!

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:41.960
This is my bento box.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.330
If you make a cute bento,
your bento box has to be cute.

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.800
I also got a couple of shape cutouts,

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.730
including this panda face one,

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:50.960
flowers, star cutouts,

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:52.980
and some cute faces.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:56.810
The bento box materials also
came with a pair of tweezers

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:57.950
and a pin.

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.650
I don't know what this
pin is gonna be used for.

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:02.230
The next thing was to buy ingredients.

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:05.200
I got carrots, I got tomatoes, kale,

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.810
cheese, ham, and sausages, rice,

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:11.340
seaweed, and some tofu skin.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:12.173
Let's get started.

00:01:12.173 --> 00:01:14.060
So I'm gonna start off
with the little sausages.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:16.490
We're gonna create little octopuses.

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:19.400
I'm supposed to just cut eight feet out.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:20.740
I tore his leg.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:21.860
I don't know how I already messed up.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:23.400
Maybe I should do this.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:24.723
This is not safe.

00:01:24.723 --> 00:01:26.370
(gasps)

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:27.580
Eight legs.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:29.700
I'm also gonna prep the eggs.

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:32.760
We're gonna make an egg omelette.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:34.890
A lot of bento boxes that
I saw on the internet

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:35.723
include this.

00:01:35.723 --> 00:01:38.290
It looks pretty and it's
a great source of protein.

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:41.810
I'm gonna add some dried vegetables.

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:47.180
I am like the clumsiest
person in the world.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:48.610
Wait, it's been 20 minutes?

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:50.020
That's because I dropped stuff.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:52.460
It'll all be a breeze from here, I'm sure.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:54.290
Alright sausages.

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:55.960
Looks like a little octopus.

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:00.100
Alright, I think that's done.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:02.470
Just gonna let them
cool down a little bit.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.650
Next up, make the egg omelette.

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:06.820
I've only done this like two times before.

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:08.240
Please don't burn.

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:09.950
Slowly fold this up.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:12.013
Oh my god.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:14.170
Then we gotta do it again.

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:17.680
I really want to get that
nice layered oval shape

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:20.070
that I see in the bento box videos.

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:24.250
Egg omelette!

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:26.720
We have the first two things done.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:28.560
So what I'm gonna try and do right now

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:30.480
is to shape little rice balls.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:31.313
Oh my god.

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:33.560
The rice is all caught in my hand.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:35.980
Help me help you become human beings.

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:36.870
Squish.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:39.150
We have our rice balls.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:40.460
So now what I'm gonna try to do

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:43.010
is to form little hats with this,

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:44.380
put it on top of the rice ball.

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:46.460
Think of like a tofu skin beanie.

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:47.920
We want to do something like this.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:50.470
This is not my trick, I
learnt it from YouTube guys.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.050
This is slippery.

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:54.790
Not as quick as I thought it would be.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:56.830
I'm gonna try to put the beanies
on the little rice balls.

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:57.920
Put that in there.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:01.500
Now it looks like a little hat!

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:03.330
Keeping the rice ball warm.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:07.090
I'm gonna cut out faces for
both the rice ball beings

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:08.560
and also the hats.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:11.180
So I'm gonna use the ham and the cheese

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:13.200
and then for the little details,

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.600
I'll have to cut it out using seaweed.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:15.680
This should be pretty simple.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:17.480
It's just cutting shapes out, right?

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:21.200
How do I get this out?

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.800
This is what this is for, right?

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:26.250
Oh yes.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:27.600
Perfect cheese circle.

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:29.520
It's like glue.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:31.510
Mayo is my glue right now.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:32.790
There we go.

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:39.710
I feel like these beanies
are giving up on me too.

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:43.946
Okay, I'm not touching it again.

00:03:43.946 --> 00:03:46.160
I don't want to destroy it.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:48.810
Then we're gonna do the eyes
for the little sausages.

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:54.950
My hands are shakin'.

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:57.710
Looks like eyeballs.

00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:58.630
They're kinda creepy looking.

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:00.700
I'm just gonna cut out some cheeks.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:02.100
Here we go.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:03.500
They're not the best looking things,

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:04.660
but they look presentable.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:07.070
This is taking a lot more
time than I thought it would.

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:08.520
But we're making good progress.

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.410
So I got a piece of seaweed.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:13.070
We're gonna try cutting out these faces.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:16.920
Nope, didn't make a dent in it.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:20.870
Trying the other face.

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:23.810
How long did I do this for?

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:24.740
It should work.

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:26.100
Amazon said they would work.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.540
Amazon never lies.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:30.030
How about with metal?

00:04:32.008 --> 00:04:34.020
(gasps)

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:34.910
I just broke it.

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:38.293
Nope.

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:44.340
This is my backup and
if this doesn't work,

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:47.712
I'm gonna run out and get
something else, I don't know what.

00:04:47.712 --> 00:04:49.045
Fingers crossed.

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:56.250
That sounds promising.

00:04:58.203 --> 00:04:59.960
Ayy!

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:00.980
Yes!

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:01.813
Yeah!

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:04.930
Trim the mouths.

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:06.280
My hands are legit shaking.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:09.780
There we go.

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:12.475
First mouth.

00:05:12.475 --> 00:05:13.550
Yay!

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:19.160
I need me some eyes right now.

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:24.370
Can he just have bigger eyes?

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:25.620
Because I can't cut.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:28.793
I for--

00:05:29.986 --> 00:05:31.800
(laughs)

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:33.640
Did that eye just fly out?

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:35.130
What?

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:37.600
How is it possible that
people do this every day?

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:41.313
No!

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:54.590
They look cute, right?

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:56.880
Yes!

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:58.319
Yeah!

00:05:58.319 --> 00:06:00.140
Sorry, I'm too excited.

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:02.490
Now I just gotta finish
off these sausage eyes.

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:07.000
Guys,

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:07.833
the octopus

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:09.910
has arrived.

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:12.620
Oh, yes.

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:14.910
I'm just gonna cut up the egg,

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:16.510
cut up the carrots,

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:17.820
and we're gonna put them all together.

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:19.130
I am so tired.

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:20.770
My back hurts.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:22.910
But I feel so accomplished.

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:25.280
Let's assemble.

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:26.650
Put some kale in.

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:29.880
Start by putting in the little people.

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:33.020
We're gonna put in the eggs,

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:37.030
and then we're gonna put
in the little sausages,

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:41.130
cherry tomatoes,

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:43.790
last thing, the pretty flower carrots.

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:46.533
And there you have it!

00:06:46.533 --> 00:06:47.690
It's kind of cute.

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:48.670
I'm pretty proud of myself.

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:50.230
I spent two and a half hours.

00:06:50.230 --> 00:06:52.160
I did not expect to be here for so long.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:54.580
Big shout out to people
who do this every day.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.140
So much respect for you.

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:57.550
Will I ever do this for my kids?

00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:58.383
No.

00:06:58.383 --> 00:06:59.570
I am done.

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:00.580
I'm done.

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:01.550
So this was fun.

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:02.940
Do I want to eat this?

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:04.740
No, because I think
it's a little too cute.

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:06.060
Let me know what you think.

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:07.390
Should I do this again?

00:07:07.390 --> 00:07:08.223
Please say no.

00:07:08.223 --> 00:07:10.680
And yeah, thank you for watching me fail.

